{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/993119-human-antagonists-nothing-supernatural-just-evil-people","id":993119,"title":"Human Antagonists: Nothing supernatural, just evil people","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-25T15:19:27-07:00","id":993119,"title":"Human Antagonists: Nothing supernatural, just evil people","content":"After marathoning Slasher flicks for the last couple of days, i was thinking about making a list for Human Antagonists, from people who are plain evil to those who belive in &quot;The Greater Good.&quot; , psychos, sociopaths or just mean people for your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:44:09-07:00","id":993140,"title":"","content":"in vampire or Werewolf their basicly just a chance for the protaganists to play vigilante.<br /> <br /> Finding a mundane child molestor or mass murderer, might be a good role playing opportunity, if you want to give your charachter the chance to play god.<br /> <br /> but is not going to be a combat challenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:53:59-07:00","id":993149,"title":"","content":"Not every mortal antagonist is going to be evil. Many of them are going to be authorities that are investigating illegal activity, like assaults that are vampire feedings or vandalism that is werewolf sabotage. Even so, I often have my most powerful enemies being mundane mortals who are wealthy and powerful enough to hire supernatural creatures as their pawns. There is a reason for the Masquerade, and I have often usen ruthless mortals often prove the reason.<br /> <br /> In one of my games, I had a corporate CEO discover and hire hundreds of female 15th generation vampires for high class escort work. He paid them ten points of Animal blood, and one point of Human blood per evening, as well as $500 a night, for acting as his spies. Their Kindred Disciplines, and other abilities, made them superior spies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 10-25-2016, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T17:03:14-07:00","id":993180,"title":"","content":"I think him being able find that many 15th gens is , to be quite frank, ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Kindred dont ADVERTISE their generation.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T17:25:04-07:00","id":993186,"title":"","content":"Vile acts in Werewolf tends to call or feed pretty nasty spirits. A 'slasher' type murderer is often a type of spirit-enfused psycho. This fits in with Werewolf's worldview, and (from a meta-game standpoint) helps beef up an otherwise puny mortal. A Garou fighting a mockery is a more interesting physical conflict than a Garou slaughtering a depraved but weak human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T17:44:54-07:00","id":993192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/993119-human-antagonists-nothing-supernatural-just-evil-people?p=993186#post993186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vile acts in Werewolf tends to call or feed pretty nasty spirits. A 'slasher' type murderer is often a type of spirit-enfused psycho. This fits in with Werewolf's worldview, and (from a meta-game standpoint) helps beef up an otherwise puny mortal. A Garou fighting a mockery is a more interesting physical conflict than a Garou slaughtering a depraved but weak human.</div> </div> </div> </div>i was thinking on the opossite. usually the Slashers are enfused by spirits, but what about normal people who do horrible acts with out an &quot;Spirit&quot; intervention?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:17:18-07:00","id":993207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/993119-human-antagonists-nothing-supernatural-just-evil-people?p=993192#post993192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i was thinking on the opossite. usually the Slashers are enfused by spirits, but what about normal people who do horrible acts with out an &quot;Spirit&quot; intervention?</div> </div> </div> </div>even if they did those things of their own accord they could draw the attention of a Bane.<br /> <br /> if not, once they come to a garous notice they will &quot;Disappear&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:57:54-07:00","id":993236,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily. There are really violent things happening in the world of Werewolf. Even werewolves that are serial killers or genocidal maniacs themselves and with no traces of corruption. So, I don't think this reasoning proposed to not be valid. The setting does have place for genuine evil not being &quot;tainted&quot; by the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And for some Garou not caring at all about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:02:18-07:00","id":993240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/993119-human-antagonists-nothing-supernatural-just-evil-people?p=993236#post993236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily. There are really violent things happening in the world of Werewolf. Even werewolves that are serial killers or genocidal maniacs themselves and with no traces of corruption. So, I don't think this reasoning proposed to not be valid. The setting does have place for genuine evil not being &quot;tainted&quot; by the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And for some Garou not caring at all about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why, though? As pervasive as the Wyrm is in the cities, why wouldn't spirits of violence or murder be drawn to the actions of an abuser or murder like a shark to blood? Doesn't mean the person is tainted or a fomori by defacto, but on the other side of the Gauntlet there is likely to be all sorts of gribblies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:36:57-07:00","id":993256,"title":"","content":"The question isn't why, but why not. If you want, do it. The OP is about the possibility of playing without the Wyrm being an issue in this case. The setting allows, and that's all. There is no reason to choose that, but he want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:32:49-07:00","id":993282,"title":"","content":"I like using the Corruption trait from Outcasts. I give Vampires and Humans an effective Corruption equal to (10-Humanity) for the purposes of Garou detecting them as evil (I have used 10-Corruption to determine the effective Humanity of Garou for game mechanics purposes, when I have not made them take Humanity and Virtues).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T00:08:35-07:00","id":993359,"title":"","content":"Even a puny mortal can pose a challenge, if need be even in combat.<br /> <br /> Humans aren't strong predators with natural weapons. But they rule the planet. Even in the WoD most nightfolk abide to some sort of masquerade to prevent their extinction by hordes of puny mortals.<br /> <br /> Preparation, outwitting, traps hidden in traps are some methods.<br /> Tools are also possible. (Super strong Garou/Vampire/whatever vs 1 metric ton of metal piloted by an evil stuntdriver)<br /> And last but not least: numbers<br /> <br /> Your pack of garou is not up to an easy victory if outnumbered 5 to 1 against professional fighters armed with military grade weaponry.<br /> <br /> Against vampires even normal folks work. Obviously the challenge is not so much a physical one but one against the beast, your humanity and the masquerade. If you loose control over your beast then you slaughter the mob risking humanity and a masquerade breach.<br /> <br /> I could go on...<br /> <br /> To summarize: humans are perfect antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T05:33:46-07:00","id":993447,"title":"","content":"They can also fade into the background fairly quickly. While there are powers that will warn you of an ambush, it is hard to escape when you are already surrounded by a crowd that ends up being your enemies. Of course, Garou have an emergency crowd suppression technique: Delirium (though they are loathe to use it because of the Veil).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T05:44:52-07:00","id":993450,"title":"","content":"Concerning Mages, sleeper antagonists shouldn't be overlooked either.<br /> <br /> Witch hunters and investigators (be they private, Arcanum, or governmental) can be a pain in the ass for Mages, since they can have considerable resources (in the case of witch hunters, we're talking about folk like the Society of Leopold), tenacity, and that most onerous quality: Idealism. They think they're doing the right thing by snooping into a Mage's affairs, upsetting their place in society, and trying to kill (or convert) them. Sometimes, they even have a point. A Technocrat looks a lot like a corrupt official or foreign spy, and a Traditionalist is not too dissimilar to a cult leader (indeed, many Mages take the Cult background, meaning the comparison is right on the money). Some sleepers have very good reason to oppose Mages.<br /> <br /> And that's just the ones who try to be covert. Sleepers can oppose Mages publicly too. An antagonist doesn't need to be a villain, just a person whose interests run against the protagonist's. Consider the head of the PTA, who thinks the local Verbana coven is a threat to the city's moral values. Or how about the head of the city's board of mental health, who looks at the local Dreamspeaker and sees a person suffering from obvious mental illness. The shaman is running around waving bones, cross-dressing, and talking to voices no one can hear. And that's not even getting into what the shaman needs to do to make his spirit allies happy. Far as the authorities are concerned, this guy is a lunatic, and would be best served being taken to a mental hospital. Obviously, they wouldn't do that if they didn't think the shaman was dangerous - the streets of major cities run thick with mentally ill homeless that no one pays attention to otherwise. But...well, the shaman is a player character, so try to guess what sort of antics they get into...<br /> <br /> Or how about very personal opponents? A Hermetic with a university job gets into a rivalry with another professor. A pot-dealing Ecstasy Cultist having his territory invaded by another dealer. Another martial arts school opening up across the street from the Akashic's dojo, not only siphoning business but also teaching students dangerous lessons. A Euthanatos right-to-die activist stymied by opponents in the state legislature, who are against doctor assisted suicide. A Verbana parent whose children are being shunned, because their neighbors don't want their kids interacting with the Wiccans. A young Virtual Adept struggling with that most heinous of hells: high school politics. A local church giving religion in a community a bad name, by being extremist in their hatred (think Westboro Baptist), giving the local Choristers all sorts of grief. The Etherite's wife, who thinks he should stop the whole &quot;lone mad scientist against the world&quot; angle, and use his talents for real science. (&quot;I don't know why you're so antagonistic at this 'Technocracy'. I think it sounds like a stable, respectable employer. Plus, I bet they pay better. Sigh...what do I tell my mother?&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T05:53:33-07:00","id":993452,"title":"","content":"To continue, the Mage Guide to the Traditions gives us the antagonistic Background, Skeptics. Instead of having a Cult that gives you extra dice on your magick rolls and can make things coincidental, Skeptics are sleeper witnesses so potent they <i>subtract </i>dice from the magick pool. These can be anything from nosy neighbors, co-workers, fans, members of the Mage's own congregation, or even family. And because their presence is both public and publicly tied to the Mage, it can be difficult to deal with them the usual way (assuming the Mage doesn't have personal reasons for not taking them out).<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the Skeptics could be the Cult of a rival Mage (or mundane cult leader, to fit with the theme of the thread), who aren't disbelieving of the Mage's powers, but ardently pray against their efforts (which is mechanically as detrimental as disbelief). This can even create an interesting twist in a chronicle, as the cabal fights and kills a rival Mage, only for their Cult to persist and have an intense desire to see the cabal fail. Depending on how potent the old cult leader was - and how big their congregation was - the Skeptics the cabal gains could amount to a greater overall threat than their leader ever was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T08:16:51-07:00","id":993500,"title":"","content":"The thing I like about plain mortal bad guys is logic. Vamps are probably the most populous of the supernaturals being easy to create. I think it mentioned somewhere that the Cam likes to keep it at 1 part per 100k, but it's probably way over crowded so 1 Vamp for every 50 k or even 10k humans, and that on the assumption that the most populous species is overcrowded by their own standards. If there weren't plenty of Humans being bad without help, no amount of supernatural would be able to make the WOD actually all that dark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T12:41:37-07:00","id":993640,"title":"","content":"I do not think a ratio of 1:10,000 would be sustainable (though I personally use 1:50,000 in the USA myself). At 1:10,000, there would be an estimated 10,000 Sabbat members and, with them each killing an average of one human per week, that would mean over 500,000 humans killed by vampire attacks alone (12.5% of the annual deaths in the USA, which would make it the third largest killer of people in the USA, after heart disease and cancer). I do not think that you could hide vampire attacks with that level of butchery, as the federal government would be motivated to discover the reasons behind the attacks. If nothing else, the sheer level of vampire hunter activity would reduce the vampire population to something more manageable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T22:55:23-07:00","id":993906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/993119-human-antagonists-nothing-supernatural-just-evil-people?p=993186#post993186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vile acts in Werewolf tends to call or feed pretty nasty spirits. A 'slasher' type murderer is often a type of spirit-enfused psycho. This fits in with Werewolf's worldview, and (from a meta-game standpoint) helps beef up an otherwise puny mortal. A Garou fighting a mockery is a more interesting physical conflict than a Garou slaughtering a depraved but weak human.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not necessarily, given the existence of groups such as DNA and Dead Man's Hand. T.F. MacNeil, of the Pentex First Teams, was also hyped up significantly in Rage: Warriors of the Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T23:09:08-07:00","id":993912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/993119-human-antagonists-nothing-supernatural-just-evil-people?p=993906#post993906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But not necessarily, given the existence of groups such as DNA and Dead Man's Hand. T.F. MacNeil, of the Pentex First Teams, was also hyped up significantly in Rage: Warriors of the Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good points, but I feel like the challenges offered by DNA are perfect examples of the challenges human antagonists can present outside of direct combat- their skullduggery can lead to all sorts of problems for Garou later down the line.<br /> <br /> As for the likes of MacNeil, this may be a case of the exception proving the rule. Those First Team humans better have Batman-levels of preparedness, otherwise they are getting pureed even easier than the rest of the freakshows and horrors on Pentex's frontline.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T10:58:34-07:00","id":994107,"title":"","content":"I think that many of the normal people throughout history were evil, but we tend to embrace a subjectivistic ethics that erroneously excuses the crimes and the sins of our ancestors (perhaps because we unconsciously desire someone in the future to excuse our present sins). <br /> <br /> Throughout history, men purchased female slaves to rape and made them do housework when their owners were too busy or too tired to victimize them, so any man who owned slaves would have certainly been evil. It is something that is often ignored in historical fiction and historical settings, that the vast majority of men were allowed to rape their children, slaves, servants, wives, etc because of the principle of masculine domination. <br /> <br /> We apologize for their behavior, attempting to state that they did not know better, but it untrue. We know, from the writings of the Ancient Greeks and the Ancient Chinese, that our ancestors knew better, they just preferred to do evil rather than to do good because the rewards for doing evil were so high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}